    "rationale": "The shown RTL (lines 170-180) is a synchronous counter register (cycle_counter) with a trivial reset/hold/increment mux feeding its D input. That mux logic feeds back into the SAME register on the next edge \u2014 it is not on the reported path at all. The reported path instead starts at this register's Q output (stage 0, clk-to-q = 0.080 ns) and then runs through 12 unattributed combinational cells (NOR4, NAND4, OAI22, NOR2, AOI211, AND3, AND3, NAND3, then a chain of three XOR2s and a NOR3) before landing on a DFFR_X1 in rtl/vendor/async_fifo/rtl/wptr_full.v:52. The XOR2 chain and the NOR3 preceding a write-pointer flop are characteristic of gray-code encoding / almost-full comparison logic inside the async FIFO's write-pointer block, not of anything in uart_rx.v. None of that combinational structure appears in the scope I was given \u2014 uart_rx.v:170-180 contains only the register itself, no interposed combinational logic to retime across, and no expression to restructure. RETIME is unavailable because there is no register inside the combinational chain to move (the only register in scope is the path's startpoint, and moving it would change when cycle_counter itself updates for every other consumer, which is out of scope to verify). RESTRUCTURE is unavailable because the logic that would need shortening lives entirely outside this file. PIPELINE is unavailable to attempt safely here because inserting a cut register requires seeing the wptr_full.v gray-code/compare logic to pick a safe cut point and to identify every reconvergent signal (e.g. the full-flag comparison) that would need matching delay \u2014 none of which is visible in this scope. Therefore NO_FIX is the correct, safe answer for this scope.",
